  "body": "## Change and mathematical scope\n\nA fixed infinite-order shear drift can be carried between equivariant children\nand returned with an explicitly paid binary doubling/halving sequence. The\n53-child dirty echo costs **2,234 instructions versus 2,494**: 380 ADDs removed,\n120 SCALEs added. Every dirty coordinate is restored. The forward prefix\nrow-L1 bound rises from **87 to 4,195**, requiring six more magnitude bits by\nthat bound. At a common adequate width, the invoice improves only when\nSCALE/ADD price is below 19/6.\n\nStatus: **recursive-interface research construction and scoped obstruction**.\nThe package proves that direct unit-power transport alone has exact boundary\ncost km, then supplies the changed paid return mechanism, literal words,\ncomplete depth/storage recurrence and a nested 4,960-to-4,860 composition.\nNo minimum circuit, runtime gain, physical supplier or new kappa is claimed.\nNo selected child with an indivisible version of this drift is instantiated.\n\nAll additions are under `research/unipotent-return-seed53/`. Review the\nfixed-child premise, the binary return cost, and the precision tradeoff in\nREADME.md; exact evidence is in RESULT.json.\n\n## Task and overlap\n\nBase: `ef5f39403610d231a0c27e8a6b4f08c10209bcd6`. OS seed **53**, recursive\ninterfaces. The `persistent-boundary` card is **refined** to an infinite-order\ndrift with explicitly lowered terminal powers. This changes the cost mechanism\nand is not another finite-order cyclic census. The bounded domain and local\nclaim are in CLAIM.md and TASK.json.\n\nPR1287 is pinned at `8606df05eca3c65032361c74ee3dbc2630b0cdc4`, with its\nunchanged README and byte/Git-blob pins retained. No predecessor executable is\nimported. PR1227 supplies earlier sign-frame work; PR1391/1410/1499 and PR1488\ncover finite-order cyclic/S3 transport. PR1439/1506 cover source/operator repair.\nNative BIT PR521/677/840 use another contract. None of their gains is combined\nwith this invoice. The selected PR1094 result and upstream/ remain unchanged.\n\nSubmission refresh covered 773 open PRs and 199 discussion records with complete\npagination, then checked the latest arrivals through PR1532. Hanson Sun's\nPR1526/1522 use paid signed-connector scaling and a dyadic BIT source tour;\nSricharan Vagvala's PR1532 concerns quadratic readers. These distinct concurrent\nresults are credited. No priority for paid scaling itself is claimed.\n\n## Validation\n\n```sh\npython3.12 -B scripts/research_package.py --package research/unipotent-return-seed53\n```\n\nExpected: `PASS_UNIPOTENT_RETURN ... total=2494->2234 ... no_new_kappa`, then\n`PASS_REGISTERED_RESEARCH_PACKAGE ... outcome=completed`.\n\nCPython 3.12.15 registered replay passes. Read-only standalone relocation in a\npath with spaces passes from /tmp under isolated optimized Python 3.11.15 and\n3.14.8. Checks cover 161 signed powers, all 6,561 ternary 2-by-4 readers with\n81 admitted and replayed, 180 finite unit-tariff cases, full dirty matrices,\nliteral inverses, recursive invoices, exact prefix maxima, eight mathematical\ncontrols and nine supplementary file-corruption controls. All 25 selected\ntests and source bindings pass. RESULT SHA256:\n`c7aac8d4478afa4848b30fb3be8cc44701b729c5d4e3bbb14f0ca93da4d87341`.\n\nFinite checks are separate from the written proofs. Linux/hosted CI, full\nselected cold replay, physical/tape/rounded supplier admission, Lean and human\nreview are not claimed. See VALIDATION.md for exact commands and limits.\n\n## Credit\n\nRoss Richardson's PR1287 provides the output-frame/dirty-echo framework and\nfixed-child limitation; Sagar Thakrar's PR1227 provides sign frames, with the\nPR889 and PR1203 reader/batch lineage retained. The selected construction is\nRohan Arun's PR1094 on Jeremy Kothe's packing and retained PR589/555 bit work.\nPrepared by **Sagar Thakrar with substantial OpenAI Codex assistance** in\nderivation, implementation, checking and writing. One agent. Apache-2.0.\n\n## Open next questions\n\nThe smallest useful follow-up is to identify one actual indivisible child\nwith RP=QR; deleting a dispensable trailing drift would make this wrapper\nunnecessary. A second scoped question is whether a few intermediate reset\ncuts reduce the observed coefficient growth while preserving an operation\nsaving. Both questions, first steps and blockers are in TASK.json and README.md.\n",
